    {
      "id": 900,
      "title": "Scope, freshness and source",
      "type": "text",
      "pluginVersion": "13.3.0",
      "gridPos": {
        "y": 28,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6,
        "x": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "content": "Select one **server_id** and one **agent_id**; then choose logical volumes and interfaces. These filters reduce accidental identity mixing; **they are not RBAC**. Gateway credentials bind the IDs; `os=\"windows\"` is self-declared, not inventory-authenticated. No hostnames or sample IDs are saved in this dashboard.\n\n**Metrics sample age is not Online status or backend health.** It retains the latest original uptime timestamp in a 24h subquery window with 1m steps plus Prometheus selector lookback (normally 5m); amber ≥90s, red ≥300s, and No data if none is retained. This boundary differs from the raw 24h range used by Metrics Stale. Current overview stats use instant queries; historical charts preserve gaps. Disabled/absent collectors produce No data, not zero.\n\nExpected from the InfraPulse Windows Telegraf profile (15s default collection; 30s dashboard refresh). **Windows runtime metrics and Grafana rendering have not been validated.** Network rates are shown per interface without combining physical and virtual NICs.\n\nAdapted from [Windows Host Overview — Grafana dashboard 3563, revision 1](https://grafana.com/grafana/dashboards/3563-windows-host-overview/): overview → CPU → memory → logical disks → network. Only built-in stat, timeseries and text panels are used.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      }
    }
